  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electric Boat obligated $11.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 333 awards, with an average award size of $34.8M. Obligations are down 45.8% year over year. Year-by-year obligations show volatility: FY21 totaled $8.7B, FY22 totaled $9.4B, FY23 totaled $10.8B, FY24 totaled $8.6B, FY25 totaled $21.4B, and FY26 totaled $11.6B. Engineering Services is the largest NAICS market in FY2026 to date at $7B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $4.6B. Smaller NAICS entries include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $3.4M and Instruments and Related Products Manufacturing for Measuring, Displaying, and Controlling Industrial Process Variables at $2.4M. The mix of large engineering and shipbuilding obligations alongside much smaller specialized manufacturing and R&D lines reflects where federal spend concentrated in the current fiscal year to date. These totals are contract obligations except where tables list award-value or total contract values explicitly.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did Electric Boat's obligations change compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Electric Boat's obligations fell 45.8% year over year in FY2026 to date. Fiscal-year totals show FY25 obligations of $21.4B and FY26 obligations of $11.6B. Prior-year totals were $8.7B in FY21, $9.4B in FY22, $10.8B in FY23, and $8.6B in FY24. These figures are contract obligations for each fiscal year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Electric Boat's largest product and service markets this fiscal year to date?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market at $7B in FY2026 to date. Ship Building and Repairing is the second-largest market at $4.6B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is listed at $3.4M, and Instruments and Related Products Manufacturing for Measuring, Displaying, and Controlling Industrial Process Variables is listed at $2.4M. Other smaller manufacturing markets range from $1.5M down to $464K."
      }
    ]
  },
